+### Sileo-style Sources / Packages / Scripts revision — 2026-10-20
+
+Use exactly these English navigation labels in both languages: Sources, Packages, Scripts. The dedicated Plugin browser uses three phone tabs and the same three iPad sidebar destinations. Keep Interceptor traffic capture outside this browser. No Featured, New, rankings, recommendation service, account or separate global-search tab. Primary visual reference: https://getsileo.app/ (official phone/iPad gallery). Use an original composition and inline SVG glyphs; do not reuse Sileo branding.
+
+Sources lists repository icons, names and URLs. Add Repository opens the added repository's Manifest catalog after metadata fetch. The catalog leads with a repository header and accessible local search of names and purposes, then compact icon-led package rows. Search shows a result count and a clear action; distinguish no match, empty catalog, loading and fetch failure. Existing cached catalog survives update failure. Repository URL and catalog search are permitted navigation inputs; Plugin settings, JSON and source remain read-only.
+
+Packages lists added Manifest bundles, showing enabled/disabled state and version/update facts. Add means import, leaves the Manifest disabled, and reveals a Packages link plus Enable. Addition and activation remain separate; explicit Enable with OK replaces an older active revision of the same family. Versions are SemVer values, never package counts. Sources registration/refresh never adds all packages or enables one.
+
+Scripts lists metadata for files grouped under their owning Manifest; neither a file listing nor a tab opens source automatically. A selected file opens full-screen read-only source with Done on phone and iPad. No file-level activation, code editor or configuration editor. Normal Sources, catalog and Package screens contain no inline JavaScript/JSON. Manifest JSON and Test remain explicit secondary destinations.
+
+Visual components: large native navigation titles; original square colored SVG icons; compact catalog rows with name, concise purpose, state and chevron; a package detail hero with icon, name and compact pill action; quiet version facts below. Destructive Disable is a restrained outlined/text action, not a full-width red banner. Supplemental explanations remain short Section footers. Shared Manifest shell/components are defined once in src/manifest-components.ts and listed in the component catalog before screen composition. Existing six workflow designs and adoption records are untouched.
+
+Mocks are self-contained clickable design fixtures, not real repository import/network/activation evidence. Navigation and local search work; add/enable state transitions use explicit fixture links without persisting app data. Keep JA/EN, phone 402×874, landscape iPad 1180×820 and light/dark variants. Native implementation, keyboard/IME, VPN and screenshot regression verification follow concrete design selection.
+
+Browser-only prototype state travels in the navigation URL's demo parameter to keep catalog, Packages and Scripts consistent inside the Viewer's sandbox. It contains synthetic fixture IDs/versions only, never app data, repository content or real activation; no browser storage or sandbox relaxation is used. Each direct state fixture seeds its declared sample; capture contexts are isolated. Initial Packages/Scripts show the file-imported Local example only.
